      {
        "id": 2885536,
        "name": "Syzygium",
        "username": "Syzygium",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/syzygium/{size}/431744_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-06-06T19:14:29.124Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Peepinglee\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"512453\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/eveonline/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/peepinglee/48/500560_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Peepinglee:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We bring new players into the game in our corp</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>In this case you simply don’t need your own structures which you can’t really defend anyway. Just rent an office on an NPC station and save a lot of costs, have all your assets stored safely and absolutely no worries about wardecs.</p>\n<p>I really don’t get why people who are unable to muster a strong fighting force and want to be left alone insist they <em>need</em> Upwell Stations in Highsec. They don’t. NPC stations offer all services you need for a Newbro Corp.</p>",
